## Quick start

Install the chart with a single storage node:

```sh
helm install vmestimator vm/victoria-metrics-estimator
```

Configure vmagent to replicate remote write traffic to:

```text
http://vmestimator-storage-vmestimator:8490/cardinality/api/v1/write
```

Cardinality estimations are exposed at `http://vmestimator-storage-vmestimator:8490/metrics`.

Each storage node maintains estimations only for the data it received, so enable select nodes to run several storage nodes:

```sh
helm install vmestimator vm/victoria-metrics-estimator --set storage.replicaCount=3 --set select.enabled=true
```

Select nodes query all storage nodes and expose merged estimations at `http://vmestimator-select-vmestimator:8490/metrics`, while storage nodes expose local estimations at `/cardinality/metrics`. The storage Service is headless, so remote write requests are sent to all storage nodes resolved by its DNS name. See the [vmestimator documentation](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/vmestimator/) for architecture and vmagent configuration details.

